-- A made-up Licensing Act.
--
--   s 3  A licensee shall not trade within 100 metres of a school.
--   s 5  Subject to section 3, a licensee may trade between 8am and 10pm.
--
-- This encoding says "Subject to section 3" in section 5's own words, and then
-- never asks section 3 anything: the permission answers TRUE at noon whatever
-- the distance to a school.

GIVEN metres IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 — the premises are within 100 metres of a school` metres MEANS
    metres LESS THAN 100

@ref Licensing Act s 5 — "Subject to section 3, a licensee may trade between 8am and 10pm."
GIVEN hour IS A NUMBER, metres IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5 — a licensee may trade` hour metres MEANS
        "Subject to section 3,"
    ... "a licensee may trade between 8am and 10pm."
    ... hour AT LEAST 8 AND hour AT MOST 22

-- Noon, 50 metres from a school. Section 3 forbids this; section 5 says yes.
#EVAL `s 5 — a licensee may trade` 12 50
